  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums` with the following properties:\n\n* `nums.length == 2 * n`.\n* `nums` includes `n + 1` **unique** values, `n` of which occur **exactly once** in the array.\n* Exactly one element of `nums` is repeated `n` times.\n\nOutput *the element that is repeated* `n` *times*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,3]\nOutput: 3\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [2,1,2,5,3,2]\nOutput: 2\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [5,1,5,2,5,3,5,4]\nOutput: 5\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `2 <= n <= 5000`\n* `nums.length == 2 * n`\n* `0 <= nums[i] <= 104`\n* `nums` includes `n + 1` **unique** elements and one of them is repeated exactly `n` times.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
